# Aero Snap — iOS project root .gitignore
# Patterns informed by:
#   - SNAP_SERIES_GUIDE.md §12 #6 (AppleDouble files break Windows builds)
#   - XcodeGen-managed project (project.yml is source of truth)

# === XcodeGen-generated project ===
# The .xcodeproj is rebuilt by `xcodegen generate`; project.yml is the
# source of truth. Committing the regenerated pbxproj produces noisy
# diffs and conflicts with iCloud Drive (the cause of "AeroSnap 2.xcodeproj"
# duplicates).
AeroSnap.xcodeproj/

# === Xcode build artifacts ===
DerivedData/
build/
*.xcuserdatad/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xccheckout
*.xcscmblueprint
*.moved-aside

# === Swift Package Manager ===
.swiftpm/
Packages/
Package.resolved
.build/

# === iOS sim + archive ===
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM
*.xcarchive

# === macOS metadata + iCloud cruft ===
# `.DS_Store` is harmless on macOS but creates noise.
# `._*` (AppleDouble) files break Windows builds per playbook §12 #6 —
# critical to ignore in the desktop sister project too.
.DS_Store
._*

# iCloud Drive duplicate-on-conflict naming pattern. The "AeroSnap 2.xcodeproj"
# incident (2026-05-31) showed iCloud creates " 2" copies when xcodegen
# regenerates a bundle dir mid-sync. Catch all such duplicates wholesale.
* 2.xcodeproj/
* 2.app/
* 2

# === Editor / IDE ===
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# === Python virtualenv (data-pipeline) ===
# (data-pipeline/.gitignore handles the per-file pipeline patterns)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# === Local dev caches that shouldn't ship ===
.cache/

# === Bundled SQLite (regenerated via data-pipeline/build_db.py) ===
# Excluded during dev to keep the repo light; revisit (LFS vs direct
# commit) when a release build needs it. See HANDOFF.md "How to build"
# for regeneration steps.
AeroSnap/Resources/*.sqlite
